---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { library, topics } from '../../lib/library';
const articles = await library();
---
<Base title="Topics" active="topics">
  <header class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Find your way in</p><h1>Ideas, in context.</h1><p>Explore the library by the role each idea plays. The collection starts small, with room to grow carefully.</p></header>
  <div class="topic-cards">{topics.map(topic => <a class="topic-card" href={`/topics/${topic.id}/`}><span class="eyebrow">{topic.number} <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /></svg></span></span><h2>{topic.name}</h2><p>{topic.description}</p><span class="entry-meta">{articles.filter(a => a.data.topic === topic.name).length} article · Working draft</span></a>)}</div>
  <div class="editorial-note"><span class="small-star"><svg class="asterisk" width="40" height="40" viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 4v32M4 20h32M9 9l22 22M9 31 31 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" /></svg></span><p>These are the first three topics, not a complete map of the field. More coverage is planned after editorial review.</p></div>
</Base>
